Z||000000||Klown||01-30-2001||11:38 PM||||I was just curious if any of you guys knew how much faster a manual transmission car was than an automatic.  I know there are a lot of variables especially when it comes to shifting technique but I just wanted to know in general how much faster the manuals are in the quarter mile and 0-60.||||reg||5
Z||000001||ray b||01-31-2001||12:18 AM|||| about a full sec.+ some in 1/4  ray||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||01-31-2001||09:21 AM||||stock? im sure sticks faster than slushomatic<BR>Modified with engine/trans swap. the new auto would waste stick because of the sloppy shift cables. Im pretty sure anyway, new autos are 20 times better than the old ones.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||01-31-2001||10:56 AM||||I originally owned an 86 SE with a 4-spd, I now own an 86 SE with an auto. In stock form the stick is faster by about 1 second 0-60 and almost 2 seconds in the 1/4. At present my car is slightly faster than a stock manual car. (manuals run in the mid 7's 0-60 and I'm in the high 6's, 6.8 was my best time 0-60 using a G-tech) There are many mods to get that far. (engine mods and a shift kit) A guy in our local club has a newer 4-spd auto in his car and it is faster with the newer auto than the original. Not sure by how much though. The gearing is different for the 4-spd auto and that helps a bit too. He is now having a 3.4L put in so it should be screaming soon.||||reg||1
Z||000004||TheFiero64||01-31-2001||11:10 AM||||I think the manual feels faster. + it is more fun. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
